On a round table, {n} labeled seats are arranged in a circle. A seating pattern is a binary sequence (b_1, b_2, ..., b_{n}) with b_i in {0,1}, where adjacency is taken cyclically (i.e., pairs (b_i, b_{i+1}) for i=1,...,{n}-1 and also (b_{n}, b_{1})). Among all such binary sequences, consider those that simultaneously satisfy the following:
- exactly {k} entries are 1;
- exactly {r} reverse orders occur (adjacent pair 1 followed by 0);
- exactly {s} forward orders occur (adjacent pair 0 followed by 1);
- every run of consecutive 1s has length at most {max_ones_run};
- every run of consecutive 0s has length at most {max_zeros_run}.
Positions are labeled, so rotations are considered different. How many such sequences exist?

